config BR2_PACKAGE_EMBRA_EMBEDDING_MODEL
	bool "embra-embedding-model"
	help
	  Sentence-embedding model installed read-only at
	  /usr/share/embra/models/<name>: an ONNX graph plus its
	  tokenizer, run in-process by embra-brain through tract for
	  knowledge-graph semantic retrieval (KG-02).

	  Default is BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5 (MIT, 33.4M parameters,
	  384 dimensions, ~133 MB). Everything runs locally: no API
	  key, no per-query cost, no data leaves the instance, and
	  retrieval works with the network down.

	  Staged host-side by scripts/build-image.sh (Step 3.6) into
	  vendor/embedding-model, sha256-verified before staging. An
	  operator can override the baked copy per instance by seeding
	  /embra/state/models/<name> on STATE.

	  Without this package retrieval still works — it falls back to
	  lexical matching and /embeddings reports the model missing.
